_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 3
---
order: 3
---
short_label: VI.3
---
statement: If an angle of a triangle is bisected by a straight line cutting the base, then the segments of the base have the same ratio as the remaining sides of the triangle; and, if segments of the base have the same ratio as the remaining sides of the triangle, then the straight line joining the vertex to the point of section bisects the angle of the triangle.
---
proof:

